ETHICAL ROYALTY SCALE (ERS)

Commercial users must self-assess their activity and remit a percentage of the gross revenue generated by or through the integration of the Software according to the following tiers:

TIER α (8%) – BENEFICIAL:
Projects that directly improve patient outcomes, support medical research, enable public health, or contribute to healthcare education and safety.

TIER β (15%) – NEUTRAL:
Generic healthcare SaaS, business analytics in medical contexts, or standard deployment without explicit patient benefit.

TIER Ω (30%) – CHAOS & DESTRUCTION:
Exploitation for unethical medical applications, surveillance, human experimentation without consent, or high-risk manipulations.

GENESIS CLAUSE:
For projects of extreme public health or societal impact without profit motive, the Author may grant a written waiver reducing royalties below 8%.

APEX CEILING:
Royalties will never exceed 30%, the maximum cap accepted by the Software.

